// Agent is one accredited person: a veterinarian, a livestock officer, the
// individual who physically stood in front of the animal.
//
// Separate from Authority, and the separation was forced by trying to run a
// sale. Attestation used to require the attestor to be an Authority — but an
// Authority must be an x/group account admitted by chain governance, so every
// field veterinarian would have to be an M-of-N group with a governance
// proposal behind them. In a pastoral zone that is not a high bar, it is an
// impossible one, and the transfer quorum of two would have needed two such
// groups before a single animal could lawfully change hands.
//
// So an agent is a PERSON with a plain key, accredited by an office rather
// than by governance — which is how accreditation actually works: a national
// veterinary order strikes off its own members, and it does not need a
// parliament to do it.
//
// The office that accredited an agent is recorded, because that is what the
// independence check turns on. An attestor accredited by the same office that
// holds the animal's record is not independent, and the four-party shape
// collapses back to one office deciding.
